{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bdlfqscc5","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pssfcu3ENvq4eWVHWoe5r2","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run1-repo/30c4c9ff-4497-4aa3-ad13-df2ffc73786d/tasks/bdlfqscc5.output","summary":"Background command \"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop; D=iter_0/candidate_5\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md <<'EOF'\nRefinement of `motif_stack`: people judge randomness as the log-likelihood ratio of a fair coin versus Griffiths et al.'s four-motif stack automaton (unchanged), but people differ in how much they additionally favour or disfavour alternation — each participant carries their own preference for the sequence that switches between H and T more often, drawn from a population distribution. The single change is this participant-level alternation-preference random effect, added because the critique shows the between-participant spread in choosing the more-alternating sequence (SD 0.22) is four times what a single-population model produces.\nEOF\necho motif_stack_alternation_individual > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nsrc=open('models/motif_stack.py').read()\nD='iter_0/candidate_5/candidate.py'\ndoc_end=src.index('\"\"\"',3)+3\nnewdoc='''\"\"\"Refinement of motif_stack: the four-motif stack automaton randomness score\nplus a participant-level random preference for alternation.\n\nHypothesis: people judge randomness as the log-likelihood ratio of a fair coin\nversus Griffiths et al.'s four-motif stack automaton, but individuals differ in\nhow strongly they additionally favour (or disfavour) the sequence that\nalternates more often; each participant's alternation preference is drawn from\na population distribution (non-centred). The motif-stack part is unchanged from\nmotif_stack.py; the single change is the per-participant alternation slope.\n\"\"\"'''\nsrc=newdoc+src[doc_end:]\nsrc=src.replace('MAX_SEQ_LEN = 8\\n','MAX_SEQ_LEN = 8\\n# Participant ids index the random effect directly; ids are unique across a\\n# run\\'s experiments, so the table is sized for many experiments.\\nMAX_PARTICIPANTS = 600\\n',1)\nsrc=src.replace('''        \"duplication\": np.array([f[2] for f in flags], dtype=\"int64\"),\n''','''        \"duplication\": np.array([f[2] for f in flags], dtype=\"int64\"),\n        \"alternation\": np.array(\n            [\n                (sum(1 for x, y in zip(s, s[1:]) if x != y) / (len(s) - 1))\n                if len(s) > 1\n                else 0.0\n                for s in sequences\n            ],\n            dtype=\"float64\",\n        ),\n''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    return {\n        **_unique_sequence_table(sequences),''','''    participant = np.array([int(float(row[\"participant_id\"])) for row in rows], dtype=\"int64\")\n    if participant.min() < 0 or participant.max() >= MAX_PARTICIPANTS:\n        raise ValueError(\n            f\"participant_id must lie in [0, {MAX_PARTICIPANTS}); got range \"\n            f\"[{participant.min()}, {participant.max()}].\"\n        )\n\n    return {\n        **_unique_sequence_table(sequences),\n        \"participant_id\": participant,''')\nsrc=src.replace('_PLACEHOLDER = prepare_observed([{\"sequence_a\": \"HT\", \"sequence_b\": \"HT\"}])',\n '_PLACEHOLDER = prepare_observed(\\n    [{\"sequence_a\": \"HT\", \"sequence_b\": \"HT\", \"participant_id\": 0}]\\n)')\nsrc=src.replace('''    duplication = pm.Data(\"duplication\", _PLACEHOLDER[\"duplication\"])\n''','''    duplication = pm.Data(\"duplication\", _PLACEHOLDER[\"duplication\"])\n    alternation = pm.Data(\"alternation\", _PLACEHOLDER[\"alternation\"])\n    participant_id = pm.Data(\"participant_id\", _PLACEHOLDER[\"participant_id\"])\n''')\nsrc=src.replace('''    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\n        \"p_left\",\n        pm.math.sigmoid(beta * (score[idx_a] - score[idx_b]) + side_bias),\n    )''','''    # Participant-level alternation preference (non-centred).\n    alt_mu = pm.Normal(\"alt_mu\", mu=0.0, sigma=2.0)\n    alt_sigma = pm.HalfNormal(\"alt_sigma\", sigma=2.0)\n    alt_z = pm.Normal(\"alt_z\", mu=0.0, sigma=1.0, shape=MAX_PARTICIPANTS)\n    alt_slope = alt_mu + alt_sigma * alt_z\n\n    eta = (\n        beta * (score[idx_a] - score[idx_b])\n        + alt_slope[participant_id] * (alternation[idx_a] - alternation[idx_b])\n        + side_bias\n    )\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(eta))''')\nopen(D,'w').write(src)\nEOF\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run1/repo\ntime /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_5 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"97aaa89c-2b05-4eba-b0f2-eb20fa0ad4ac","session_id":"30c4c9ff-4497-4aa3-ad13-df2ffc73786d"}
